      "claim": "Classical statistics (MLE) is a limit case of the Bayesian framework when $n \\gg d$.",
      "supported": true,
      "evidence_or_problem": "[00:53:22\u201300:53:54] You may ask me if there's a contradiction between classical statistics and Bayesian framework. So what if the statistical community is divided on two different opposing subgroups, which fight each other on each scientific conference, so frequencies versus Bayesians. And the answer is actually no. Here we consider, so this can be even proven, but here we consider posterior distribution conditioned on a large number of observations. [00:53:55\u201300:54:26] in the limit when n is much larger than d. [...] And this means that classical statistics can regard it as a limit case of Bayesian framework"
